and reverse curses

04:04.140 --> 04:04.180
We set the standard

04:04.140 --> 04:04.180
The best

04:04.140 --> 04:04.180
first twenty customers will be presented
with a memento!

04:04.140 --> 04:04.180
discount ticket

04:04.180 --> 04:04.220
Picture book level

04:04.180 --> 04:04.220
Powerful magic users

04:04.180 --> 04:04.220
Spell Shop

04:04.180 --> 04:04.220
Yoyo

04:04.180 --> 04:04.220
Nene

04:04.180 --> 04:04.220
We set the standard

04:04.180 --> 04:04.220
The best

04:04.270 --> 04:07.850
Here's some coupons for a ten percent discount off your next visit!

04:08.590 --> 04:10.480
Please rely on our services again!

05:25.990 --> 05:27.640
That's a pretty stone, isn't it?

05:28.010 --> 05:30.800
It was inside that monster from earlier.

05:31.680 --> 05:33.180
That stone belonged to my sister.

05:33.890 --> 05:36.660
She had a talent for making stone talismans.

05:38.190 --> 05:41.730
But Yoyo-san, why would the monster have something like that inside it?

05:43.510 --> 05:47.990
Her sister might have been cursed by someone...

05:47.990 --> 05:52.700
As a certain someone found out, there are even curses that can turn you into a frog.

05:54.160 --> 05:55.540
Allergies?

05:55.880 --> 06:01.640
For a reasonable price, we could even hunt them down with a curse of our own.

06:11.500 --> 06:13.130
My poor forest...

06:14.060 --> 06:15.310
Wh-Wh—

06:16.010 --> 06:19.210
What is this!?

06:31.620 --> 06:33.530
This is unforgivable!

06:33.920 --> 06:37.520
What kind of lunatic would drop something like this in front of our house!?

06:38.010 --> 06:39.620
I'll curse them to death!

06:40.140 --> 06:42.250
I wonder who would cast a curse like this...

06:42.770 --> 06:45.120
More importantly, I've never seen buildings like those either.

06:45.120 --> 06:49.500
You're right! And for that reason, I'm going to investigate it!

06:50.640 --> 06:51.890
Let's go, Bihaku!

07:10.660 --> 07:13.370
In our next segment, we travel to Yokohama

07:13.370 --> 07:17.370
where a monkey named Yoshi is on the run. He seems—

07:19.300 --> 07:20.570
Is this magic!?

07:26.160 --> 07:27.740
The spell was absorbed...

07:40.170 --> 07:42.050
I wonder if Yoyo-san is all right...

07:42.580 --> 07:45.230
She's probably just goofing off, anyway.

07:45.980 --> 07:47.630
I think I'm going to take a look, after all.

07:50.160 --> 07:51.490
I'm coming with you!

08:19.770 --> 08:21.430
What do you guys think you're...

08:21.890 --> 08:22.540
Huh?

08:23.920 --> 08:25.840
They were here just a moment ago...

08:31.210 --> 08:32.680
Yoyo-san!

08:40.060 --> 08:41.180
These markings...

08:41.180 --> 08:42.100
Yoyo-san!

08:43.060 --> 08:44.080
Nene-chan!

08:45.960 --> 08:48.540
There's something weird about this place!

08:51.750 --> 08:52.690
Take this!

08:54.920 --> 08:56.870
Yoyo-san, step out of the way!

09:01.520 --> 09:02.640
Nene-chan!

09:02.640 --> 09:03.780
Yoyo-san!

09:04.700 --> 09:05.610
Nene-chan!

09:08.940 --> 09:10.480
What's going on!?

09:35.880 --> 09:39.250
What is this!?

10:01.930 --> 10:03.360
It doesn't hurt!

10:08.210 --> 10:09.750
I've gotten bigger!

10:11.700 --> 10:13.670
And you've gotten smaller, Bihaku.

10:15.460 --> 10:18.010
Its head... spun around.

10:19.730 --> 10:21.850
Hey, it's you!

10:22.640 --> 10:25.070
Who do you guys think you are!?

10:25.070 --> 10:27.060
Huh?

10:25.800 --> 10:26.540
Wait up!

10:29.360 --> 10:30.470
Jeez!

10:33.320 --> 10:34.670
I won't let you escape!

10:36.820 --> 10:39.070
Dangerous! She's gotta be dangerous!

10:49.540 --> 10:50.030
There!

10:53.290 --> 10:54.440
Wait!

11:02.430 --> 11:03.300
Hey!

11:06.890 --> 11:08.140
What's with that girl?

11:07.520 --> 11:07.560
My Room

11:09.060 --> 11:11.770
Bro, what are you doing here?

11:14.270 --> 11:16.950
Mom and Dad are...

11:16.950 --> 11:17.820
Huh?

11:23.950 --> 11:26.090
What!? Who's that girl!?

11:33.830 --> 11:34.790
This is...

11:35.880 --> 11:36.830
A curse!

11:38.430 --> 11:40.890
What did you guys do!?

11:40.890 --> 11:41.580
Wh—

11:41.580 --> 11:42.300
"Wh"?

11:42.730 --> 11:44.350
What are those!?

11:44.350 --> 11:47.680
L-Like I said, it's Mom and Dad!

11:48.670 --> 11:50.600
Papa and Mama?

11:50.600 --> 11:53.340
Huh!? Bro, what are you talking about?

11:53.340 --> 11:54.520
It's true!

11:54.520 --> 11:55.610
All of a sudden—

11:55.920 --> 11:57.070
This is a curse—

11:58.980 --> 12:00.730
What's this!? Open a window!

12:00.730 --> 12:01.990
Window? Where?

12:19.750 --> 12:21.580
Where did the forest go!?

12:21.580 --> 12:23.090
First, who the hell are you!?

12:30.850 --> 12:33.100
I got taken to some other world!

12:40.250 --> 12:43.520
I'm Yoyo. Can I go now?

12:43.520 --> 12:45.140
No, you can't!

12:45.140 --> 12:47.840
The door and the rest of the house are completely trashed!

12:47.840 --> 12:48.920
Oh, you're right.

12:49.620 --> 12:50.100
Hoi!

12:59.250 --> 13:02.450
It doesn't quite fit the decor, but it'll have to do.

13:02.450 --> 13:04.680
Hey, can you pinch me for a sec?

13:04.980 --> 13:07.090
And, now, Yoyo will be leaving.

13:08.330 --> 13:08.960
Hey!

13:09.090 --> 13:09.600
Brother?

13:13.800 --> 13:14.940
Did I mess something up?

13:14.940 --> 13:16.290
Don't you know how doors work!?

13:16.290 --> 13:17.730
Now, now.

13:18.050 --> 13:22.650
More importantly, you said Mom and Dad were under a curse, didn't you?

13:22.650 --> 13:24.110
A curse?

13:24.110 --> 13:26.470
You're saying they had some kind of "magic" cast on them?

13:26.470 --> 13:27.630
That's right.

13:27.630 --> 13:30.050
You're really shady, you know?

13:30.050 --> 13:31.870
Magic is just smoke and mirrors!

13:31.870 --> 13:33.370
Want to bet?

13:36.600 --> 13:38.880
See? Do you believe me now?

13:39.490 --> 13:41.560
So <i>you're</i> the one behind all this!?

13:41.560 --> 13:42.790
Hold on a second.

13:42.790 --> 13:46.880
If they were cursed, can you revert them back to normal?

13:47.410 --> 13:52.590
Sure, but only if we manage to locate the source so I can dispel the curse.

13:52.590 --> 13:54.980
Could I ask you to do that?

13:56.710 --> 13:58.350
That's asking a lot...

13:58.800 --> 14:01.490
I've got other things to investigate.

14:01.490 --> 14:03.010
Please. Can't you help us?

14:08.940 --> 14:10.720
Nene-chan's talisman set!

14:14.960 --> 14:15.830
It's here!

14:16.330 --> 14:17.350
What are you doing?

14:17.750 --> 14:20.480
I'm going to try and contact Nene-chan.

14:21.040 --> 14:22.500
Who's Nene-chan?

14:22.920 --> 14:24.550
She's my little sister.

14:26.380 --> 14:27.800
This is magic, too?

14:28.510 --> 14:30.820
Nene-chan! Nene-chan!

14:30.820 --> 14:31.990
Can you hear me?

14:33.210 --> 14:34.160
Yoyo-san!

14:34.640 --> 14:35.590
Are you all right?

14:35.590 --> 14:37.180
Righter than rain!

14:37.180 --> 14:38.390
The heck is that?

14:38.390 --> 14:39.610
A frog?

14:39.610 --> 14:41.540
Such a pretty older sister.

14:41.540 --> 14:42.440
Her!?

14:43.160 --> 14:44.850
<i>I'm </i>the older sister!

14:44.850 --> 14:46.690
Who are those two?

14:47.160 --> 14:48.440
This is Spiky and Long Hair.

14:48.440 --> 14:49.570
My name is Takahiro!

14:49.570 --> 14:52.780
I'm S-Shiruga K-Kensei!

14:56.110 --> 14:57.110
I see.

14:58.010 --> 14:59.790
Takahiro-san?

15:00.120 --> 15:00.640
Yeah?

15:01.240 --> 15:05.550
So, Takahiro-san, you had a similar experience in that moving elevator box?

15:06.150 --> 15:10.970
Yeah, I woke up and left to do my morning exercises with Aki.

15:07.970 --> 15:09.470
Summer break

15:07.970 --> 15:09.470
radio

15:07.970 --> 15:09.470
calisthenics card.

15:15.560 --> 15:18.390
We got on the elevator, and suddenly, the lights went out.

15:19.310 --> 15:21.770
From there on, things stopped making sense.

15:24.670 --> 15:27.820
When it finally spit us out, she was there.

15:29.300 --> 15:33.570
Yoyo-san... The things happening in both our world and theirs...

15:34.040 --> 15:36.330
Could they be connected somehow?

15:36.610 --> 15:38.150
It seems likely.

15:38.150 --> 15:42.160
A dark magician from our world might be spreading mischief in theirs.

15:42.680 --> 15:44.960
The same one who did that to Mom and Dad?

15:44.960 --> 15:48.740
And by the way, our services don't come cheap.

15:48.740 --> 15:50.920
Huh? You're charging us?

15:50.920 --> 15:53.330
You tryin' ta get cursed again?

15:53.330 --> 15:55.290
Considering the situation, I don't think we have a choice.

15:56.400 --> 15:58.240
You're hiring us, then?

15:58.950 --> 16:00.350
We accept!

16:00.900 --> 16:01.920
All right.

16:01.920 --> 16:03.420
I'm heading out.

16:04.570 --> 16:05.750
At a time like this?

16:05.750 --> 16:09.680
I already made plans. Plus, I know next to nothing about these curses.

16:09.680 --> 16:11.860
If she can figure it out, we're all good.

16:11.860 --> 16:14.560
B-But Mom and Dad are...

16:14.560 --> 16:16.240
There's no good reason for me to stay.

16:17.630 --> 16:20.070
And besides, it's not like they're about to die.

16:21.300 --> 16:21.870
See ya!

16:21.870 --> 16:24.430
Then take Aki-chan with you!

16:26.820 --> 16:27.960
Please?

16:32.930 --> 16:34.610
You better behave!

16:35.700 --> 16:37.230
Okay, let's go!

16:40.990 --> 16:45.850
That magic vane should direct you to the magic's source.

16:49.770 --> 16:51.220
It's moving!

16:57.070 --> 16:58.520
Be careful, Yoyo-san.

17:00.330 --> 17:01.790
I'm off!

17:07.630 --> 17:08.460
She's flying...

17:37.790 --> 17:39.840
Ow! Hot! Ow, ow, ow, ow!

17:40.880 --> 17:41.790
What is this place?

17:48.390 --> 17:50.550
The source of the magic is here?

18:11.680 --> 18:13.980
I could probably use a change of clothes.

18:19.100 --> 18:20.620
It's so hot.

18:29.300 --> 18:29.940
All right!

18:42.950 --> 18:44.820
You're the girl from Spiky's house.

18:45.710 --> 18:47.540
What are you doing by yourself?

18:52.930 --> 18:54.330
That's really pretty.

18:54.900 --> 18:57.070
Do you like collecting rocks?

19:00.590 --> 19:01.950
I give them to Mama.

19:05.890 --> 19:07.900
Want me to give you a hand?

19:08.790 --> 19:13.580
Or so I said... but this doesn't look like a place where we'd find many.

19:15.670 --> 19:16.820
Are you all right!?

19:38.350 --> 19:45.660
With her green hair and green eyes,

19:45.660 --> 19:48.830
she's arrived!

19:49.540 --> 19:53.170
It's Yoyo-san! Hoi!

19:53.170 --> 19:56.960
I love Nene-chan

19:56.960 --> 20:01.000
We're the spell casting sisters of the forest

20:01.000 --> 20:04.060
Even though I'm smaller, I'm the eldest

20:04.060 --> 20:07.960
That's right, I'm Yoyo-san! Hoi!

20:07.960 --> 20:11.710
I might not be what you expect at first

20:11.710 --> 20:15.400
but I'm sure in the end you won't mind

20:15.860 --> 20:19.320
Crybabies and even caterpillars can't help but smile

20:19.320 --> 20:23.200
when I'm the one leading the fun. Hohoi!

20:23.200 --> 20:26.640
I want to make the world mine

20:26.640 --> 20:31.040
when it comes to magic, anything is possible.

20:31.040 --> 20:34.690
There isn't any magic or spell I can't do.

20:34.690 --> 20:37.960
I'm Yoyo-san! Hoi!

20:38.520 --> 20:42.130
After all, I'm the invincible magical girl.

20:42.130 --> 20:45.730
I'm Yoyo-san! Hoi!

21:08.100 --> 21:09.700
So you're a magical girl?

21:10.010 --> 21:11.220
That's right!

21:11.790 --> 21:14.080
My adventures have even been made into picture books!

21:14.080 --> 21:16.630
Wow! That's amazing, Yoyo-chi!

21:21.620 --> 21:22.590
Huh?

21:23.120 --> 21:25.010
He went to Hawaii?

21:25.010 --> 21:26.520
That's what I heard.

21:26.520 --> 21:29.770
Good for him... My family never goes anywhere!

21:29.770 --> 21:32.180
Something about a recession here...

21:32.180 --> 21:33.770
They won't buy me games, either.

21:34.300 --> 21:37.960
Since you're here, help me out a little. I can't do this alone, man.

21:37.960 --> 21:39.750
It's not my turn.

21:40.140 --> 21:41.860
Hey, let's go over there.

21:41.860 --> 21:42.730
Good idea!

21:42.730 --> 21:44.960
It <i>is</i> your duty!

21:45.870 --> 21:48.450
He's just leaving his relatives behind like that.

21:48.450 --> 21:50.870
Sweet, I got it!

21:50.870 --> 21:54.410
Item

21:50.870 --> 21:54.410
plaza

21:50.870 --> 21:54.410
card that grants wishes

21:51.440 --> 21:52.820
What's that?

21:52.820 --> 21:54.410
A cell phone game?

21:54.410 --> 21:56.220
It's a rare card!

21:56.890 --> 21:58.310
Wait, what's this?

21:58.310 --> 22:01.860
It says to type in your wish.

22:01.860 --> 22:04.010
Something like a reply?

22:04.580 --> 22:05.560
Let me see!

22:05.560 --> 22:06.290
Hey!

22:07.400 --> 22:11.680
Um... I want to go to SeaLand.

22:07.600 --> 22:08.760
Give it back!

22:15.250 --> 22:17.780
C'mon! Don't do that without asking!

22:17.780 --> 22:19.920
Now there's only five left!

22:19.920 --> 22:22.690
It's not like it'll actually come true!

22:26.210 --> 22:27.430
What the heck?

22:28.700 --> 22:28.740
Season Tickets - SeaLand Resort

22:34.080 --> 22:35.460
It did work...

22:41.630 --> 22:42.960
Is this for real!?

22:42.960 --> 22:44.340
Isn't it just a coincidence?

22:44.710 --> 22:49.090
Hey, let's test how far we can go with these wishes!

22:49.440 --> 22:50.640
Give it to me!

22:50.640 --> 22:51.850
Give it back!

22:51.850 --> 22:54.660
I want some games!

22:53.850 --> 22:55.560
Give it back already!

22:55.560 --> 22:55.680
Write your

22:55.560 --> 22:55.680
wish for someone

22:55.560 --> 22:55.680
portable

22:56.430 --> 22:56.560
I want Shibatan's Spike?

22:58.020 --> 22:58.060
Write your

22:58.020 --> 22:58.060
wish for someone

23:14.640 --> 23:15.450
What's that?

23:18.320 --> 23:19.600
Hey!

23:23.070 --> 23:24.880
Someone!

23:40.400 --> 23:41.320
What's this?

23:41.760 --> 23:43.180
Is it the same curse?

23:43.180 --> 23:44.490
One of them managed to escape.

23:45.230 --> 23:46.440
Follow it!

23:46.440 --> 23:47.980
There's a clue on it!

23:51.870 --> 23:53.070
Don't mind if I do!

24:08.320 --> 24:08.840
Let's go!

24:15.860 --> 24:17.850
That's the wrong way!

24:18.470 --> 24:19.690
Pardon the intrusion!

24:20.290 --> 24:21.430
Hey, who was that?

24:22.850 --> 24:24.490
Sorry for the disruption!

24:26.860 --> 24:29.190
So this can float on water, huh?

24:48.550 --> 24:48.630
Chinatown

25:00.020 --> 25:01.880
There's too many people!

25:03.940 --> 25:05.310
Where did it go?

25:08.980 --> 25:10.610
You're all in the way!

25:21.160 --> 25:21.830
Over there!

25:22.290 --> 25:23.710
What is this?

25:24.360 --> 25:25.660
Some kind of event?

25:41.920 --> 25:43.470
I got you now!

25:48.380 --> 25:49.600
Nice one!

25:49.600 --> 25:51.070
Spiky!

25:56.410 --> 25:57.160
Huh?

26:01.460 --> 26:02.240
Look out!

26:02.240 --> 26:03.500
This time for sure!

26:27.880 --> 26:28.370
Here.

26:34.040 --> 26:36.530
Thank you! Thank you!

26:39.630 --> 26:41.690
Yoyo! You're amazing.

26:41.690 --> 26:43.930
You can do pretty much anything with magic!

26:44.940 --> 26:49.480
That said, we still don't know how to fix Mom and Dad's situation.

26:50.340 --> 26:54.460
Spiky, why did that person look so happy?

26:54.460 --> 26:55.210
Huh?

27:07.180 --> 27:11.110
Wh-What's the meaning of this!?

27:11.110 --> 27:13.760
There's more! Why are there more!?

27:13.760 --> 27:17.830
It's not like we could just leave them out there.

27:17.830 --> 27:20.670
Wait! What happened to your clothes?

27:20.670 --> 27:22.660
Huh? Now that you mention it...

27:22.660 --> 27:23.710
I wonder why.

27:23.710 --> 27:27.870
What in the world happened? Weren't you supposed to find the person responsible for all this!?

27:28.560 --> 27:33.170
This is Teppei-kun's cell phone. And these are Mom and Dad's.

27:33.680 --> 27:35.820
They were all playing the same game.

27:36.370 --> 27:40.600
Teppei and the others got a rare card, and after their wish was granted, they turned into monsters.

27:41.130 --> 27:42.220
Rare card?

27:42.630 --> 27:45.220
I think there was even one left.

27:46.090 --> 27:46.860
Here it is.

27:47.890 --> 27:50.230
Which country's crest is this, I wonder...

27:50.900 --> 27:54.180
This is the source of power that the magic vane led us to.

27:54.180 --> 27:58.200
A curse where you turn into a monster after your wish is fulfilled, huh?

27:58.830 --> 28:01.730
You'd think that it'd be something more complicated than that...

28:03.380 --> 28:05.700
Hey, can't you just change them back?

28:06.020 --> 28:09.870
If we could convince the person who made the curse to dispel it, maybe...

28:10.780 --> 28:14.160
I'm going to do some research into those inscriptions.

28:15.540 --> 28:18.840
Yoyo-san, let's continue this tomorrow and call it a day for now.

28:19.310 --> 28:22.420
We're having grilled mini mammoths for dinner.

28:22.840 --> 28:23.840
I'm going home.

28:24.270 --> 28:26.350
You can't fix it today!?

28:26.870 --> 28:30.390
Magic, huh? I wish I could do it, too.

28:30.900 --> 28:33.310
As long as they've got magic power, anyone can.

28:33.710 --> 28:35.560
Magic power, huh?

28:35.560 --> 28:37.860
Sounds convenient but troublesome...

28:39.860 --> 28:42.340
All righty then! I'll be back tomorrow.

28:42.340 --> 28:44.990
Please! You gotta hurry up and figure all this out.

29:05.090 --> 29:05.930
Huh?

29:07.330 --> 29:08.870
What is the meaning of this!?

29:22.860 --> 29:24.870
You can't go back!?

29:25.710 --> 29:27.610
But you came here, right?

29:28.190 --> 29:30.740
Why do you think I'm researching it!?

29:31.170 --> 29:33.740
Doesn't your older sister have any ideas?

29:33.740 --> 29:36.040
I won't say it again! I'm the older sister!

29:36.550 --> 29:38.690
I'll start looking into it now.

29:39.130 --> 29:40.230
I'm counting on you.

29:42.370 --> 29:43.360
What's wrong?

29:47.800 --> 29:51.180
Now I'm hesitant about whether you can even fix things on our end.

29:51.720 --> 29:54.950
We have a one hundred percent satisfaction rate!

29:54.950 --> 29:56.580
I'll figure it out!

29:56.580 --> 29:58.020
I wonder about that...

29:58.020 --> 30:01.640
A magical girl who's unable to get back to her home world sure seems suspicious.

30:01.640 --> 30:03.610
You're making fun of me, aren't you!?

30:05.710 --> 30:07.610
Hey, what have you done!?

30:07.610 --> 30:09.200
Change me back!

30:09.960 --> 30:12.370
This is a magical heart detox.

30:14.880 --> 30:17.010
Takahiro!

30:17.010 --> 30:21.170
You can see for yourself just how dirty his heart was!

30:21.170 --> 30:23.970
Anyway, I guess I'm staying the night here.

30:26.530 --> 30:28.650
But before that, I'm starving.

30:30.340 --> 30:31.470
Allow me!

30:31.470 --> 30:34.090
Is soba all right?

30:34.090 --> 30:35.540
What's that?

30:35.990 --> 30:36.670
Instant—

30:36.670 --> 30:41.180
Stop! You'll ruin my first impressions if you give me the details now!

30:42.550 --> 30:44.040
Darn you!

30:44.040 --> 30:45.490
You've done it again!

30:45.490 --> 30:48.740
Contains a
powdered
sauce packet

30:45.490 --> 30:48.740
Yakisoba

30:45.490 --> 30:48.740
Chunky cut

30:45.490 --> 30:48.740
pork

30:45.490 --> 30:48.740
and

30:45.490 --> 30:48.740
cabbage

30:46.770 --> 30:48.740
Just add hot water and wait for three minutes.

30:49.180 --> 30:51.230
You wait? With magic—

30:51.230 --> 30:53.210
Don't underestimate the pleasure of waiting!

30:59.910 --> 31:01.790
Is that really food?

31:02.780 --> 31:04.000
Sure it is.

31:04.900 --> 31:05.630
How's this!?

31:07.860 --> 31:08.620
Wait!

31:09.010 --> 31:12.360
Without these, it's not really soba.

31:25.540 --> 31:26.410
It's complete!

31:44.730 --> 31:47.420
This is chicken soup for the soul!

31:47.420 --> 31:49.360
Chicken soup, right?

31:49.360 --> 31:50.670
It's really yummy, right?

31:51.360 --> 31:52.680
It's not chicken soup.

31:55.210 --> 31:58.270
Nene-chan has gotta try this!

32:05.100 --> 32:09.750
N-Nene-chan, today, in Yoyo's stead, I could...

32:09.750 --> 32:10.530
Sure.

32:10.530 --> 32:11.060
Huh?

32:20.480 --> 32:25.390
Everything will be all right! It's no different than if Yoyo-san had gone out to play!

32:49.070 --> 32:52.670
Look at this! It's a girl riding on a wall that suddenly appeared in Chinatown!

32:49.070 --> 32:52.070
Breaking News!

32:49.070 --> 32:52.070
A mysterious girl and

32:49.070 --> 32:52.070
giant wall in Chinatown

32:52.410 --> 32:53.560
That's me!

32:53.560 --> 32:56.560
What kind of magic is used to display this?

32:53.610 --> 32:59.820
She appears to be riding on a skateboard as if surfing.

32:56.560 --> 33:00.110
Magic? There's none of that here, it's just a TV.

32:59.820 --> 33:07.990
By coincidence one of our newscasters caught the girl in the background.

33:00.110 --> 33:01.390
TV?

33:03.830 --> 33:08.590
We caught this moment on camera!

33:03.830 --> 33:08.590
Only we have the full story

33:03.830 --> 33:08.590
behind this mysterious uproar.

33:04.520 --> 33:06.930
So this magic is called TV, huh?

33:39.350 --> 33:40.290
You're not asleep?

33:49.960 --> 33:50.040
Yoyo and the Giant Monsters

33:52.980 --> 33:56.130
Yoyo and the great fish!

33:59.810 --> 34:03.110
With the use of spells made by Yoyo-san's infinite magic power,

34:03.600 --> 34:05.140
they were able to defeat the monsters!

34:05.870 --> 34:06.660
And so—

34:07.050 --> 34:10.440
Peace returned to the Kingdom of Magic.

34:10.930 --> 34:12.280
You've heard about it!?

34:21.900 --> 34:25.550
So the tales of my adventures have even reached other worlds.

34:32.200 --> 34:33.480
Ta-da!

34:33.480 --> 34:38.050
My lightweight and convenient Yoyo-cell phone is complete!

34:38.440 --> 34:40.710
Wait. That's Dad's cell phone.

34:41.120 --> 34:43.520
I borrowed the TV magic.

34:43.520 --> 34:45.700
Wait! Are you eating yakisoba again!?

34:46.100 --> 34:49.020
With this, I can communicate with Nene-chan anytime.

34:49.530 --> 34:50.560
Nene-chan!

34:55.080 --> 34:56.870
She must be out.

34:56.870 --> 35:00.450
I did some research into that game yesterday.

35:02.190 --> 35:04.210
Looks like the Kingdom of Magic.

35:04.210 --> 35:08.240
It's a super popular game with tons of downloads.

35:08.240 --> 35:10.460
What about the people who use that rare card?

35:08.910 --> 35:14.210
Card that grants wishes

35:11.010 --> 35:14.210
So far, nothing about that at all.

35:14.800 --> 35:18.720
It's renowned for granting wishes, however.

35:19.900 --> 35:21.860
I don't get it.

35:22.310 --> 35:25.420
Why are they the only cursed ones?

35:34.690 --> 35:36.440
Where did you get this?

35:36.970 --> 35:39.430
Hey, give it back to her.

35:39.430 --> 35:42.000
This! It's a magical inscription!

35:43.100 --> 35:43.730
Huh?

35:47.850 --> 35:49.500
Mama gave it to me.

35:50.490 --> 35:51.260
Mama?

35:51.840 --> 35:55.080
No, not her. Aki is just a relative.

35:55.080 --> 35:56.990
Our uncle is busy, so we're looking after her.

35:57.740 --> 36:01.780
So why would that be on the Pez dispenser she got from our aunt?

36:01.780 --> 36:03.000
No idea.

36:03.520 --> 36:06.560
It looks a bit like one I've seen before to dispel a curse.

36:07.120 --> 36:10.490
Dispel a curse? What would our aunt...

36:10.980 --> 36:12.350
Mama's at home.

36:14.080 --> 36:15.520
Let's go check it out!

36:16.140 --> 36:17.530
Please lead me there!

36:21.030 --> 36:22.740
Here you are.

36:43.270 --> 36:44.100
This is it!

36:44.490 --> 36:45.980
The Magic of Happiness.

36:46.900 --> 36:49.170
The author is... Nao.

36:50.980 --> 36:52.180
That woman!

36:55.780 --> 36:58.190
My older sister has been missing.

36:59.270 --> 37:02.130
She had a talent for making stone talismans.

37:03.470 --> 37:06.930
Leading researcher of the Miracle Stone.

37:08.570 --> 37:13.800
Twelve years ago at the battlefields of Kenma, she got caught up in a travelling spell and the rest is unknown.

37:14.790 --> 37:16.040
This is...

37:19.290 --> 37:23.080
Over there! No, over the— I said over there, damn it!

37:30.640 --> 37:31.260
Huh!?

37:32.340 --> 37:38.360
As you can see behind me, the gate into Chinatown disappeared last night!

37:43.310 --> 37:44.390
So this is the place.

37:44.900 --> 37:47.220
Who knows what demons lurk inside?

37:47.220 --> 37:48.990
<i>You're</i> the demon here!

37:49.730 --> 37:52.720
Listen up, Spiky. Stay behind me, got it?

37:52.720 --> 37:56.710
Amateurs should— Hey. Aki-chan!

37:57.190 --> 37:58.540
Mama is in here.

37:59.290 --> 38:00.750
Hold on a sec!

38:08.880 --> 38:10.920
What? She's dead!?

38:12.550 --> 38:14.070
Keep your voice down!

38:15.860 --> 38:18.940
I think it was about a year ago... She was in some accident.

38:18.940 --> 38:21.680
Th-Then where is she now?

38:21.680 --> 38:24.980
Huh? Like I said, she's no longer in this world.

38:24.980 --> 38:27.930
No way.

38:38.430 --> 38:39.440
This is...

38:41.010 --> 38:44.450
Like I thought, she's got nothing to do with it.

38:45.090 --> 38:47.820
I've met her before. She was just a normal person.

38:48.340 --> 38:49.760
No, look.

38:50.350 --> 38:52.470
These are things from the Kingdom of Magic.

38:52.960 --> 38:54.140
Seriously!?

38:54.980 --> 38:57.690
So she really <i>was </i>dabbling in magic, after all.

38:59.150 --> 39:04.220
But even if that's true, how would a dead person cast a curse?

39:06.060 --> 39:09.660
If the curse is powerful enough, it can span for several generations.

39:12.700 --> 39:15.450
I wonder if someone's talking about me.

39:16.370 --> 39:17.950
Maybe it was Nene-chan...

39:24.700 --> 39:28.990
For the curse to be acting up now, that must mean...

39:32.920 --> 39:38.000
If Nao-san were here, she'd be able to send me home.

39:46.920 --> 39:48.050
Bifocals?

39:48.050 --> 39:49.530
Pastfocals!

39:50.140 --> 39:52.650
Let's see... one year.

40:02.560 --> 40:05.390
Huh? Where have I seen her before?

40:13.090 --> 40:14.820
E-Excuse me! Your ID—

40:14.820 --> 40:15.690
What was that?

40:16.930 --> 40:18.980
I'm sorry!

40:27.380 --> 40:28.760
Nene!

40:29.360 --> 40:31.280
Are you here, Nene?

40:32.770 --> 40:33.740
Yes!

40:34.310 --> 40:37.080
Um, please be quiet in the library.

40:37.740 --> 40:39.790
I'm sorry!

40:45.450 --> 40:48.420
Oyone-san! What are you doing here?

40:48.420 --> 40:50.630
My presence here is not what's important.

40:51.060 --> 40:53.740
I have a few questions to ask you.

41:01.880 --> 41:03.640
Did you figure anything out?

41:06.890 --> 41:09.640
It seems to be some type of magic that utilizes rocks,

41:09.640 --> 41:12.040
but it doesn't look like it can give us any clues.

41:12.750 --> 41:15.530
So she really was from the Kingdom of Magic.

41:16.560 --> 41:18.890
That means Aki is...

41:21.870 --> 41:24.250
Let's head back for now.

41:24.250 --> 41:27.430
We can ask my uncle later. He might know something.

41:27.430 --> 41:29.800
I'm starving.

41:30.100 --> 41:31.300
You're right.

41:32.470 --> 41:34.680
It's settled. Let's go get some yakisoba!

41:34.680 --> 41:36.180
Spare me your flying.

41:36.550 --> 41:38.870
What!? But it's so fast!

41:38.870 --> 41:40.430
<i>Not</i> gonna happen.

41:43.370 --> 41:44.440
What's that?

41:48.430 --> 41:51.440
Hey! Over here, over here!

41:52.840 --> 41:54.270
What happened?

41:54.720 --> 41:57.560
Apparently, it just fell out of the sky.

41:57.560 --> 42:00.830
That's right. And on top of Nils, at that.

42:01.190 --> 42:02.210
Nils!

42:03.150 --> 42:05.560
What a brittle little guy.

42:05.560 --> 42:07.430
Oyomi, do it.

42:07.890 --> 42:09.840
Well, if you say so.

42:28.720 --> 42:30.380
Good as new.

42:30.870 --> 42:33.200
A job well done, as always.

42:33.740 --> 42:37.610
So... what's all this?

42:43.380 --> 42:45.970
It'd only take a second if we flew.

42:45.970 --> 42:47.850
You could have gone by yourself.

42:48.390 --> 42:50.920
But I don't know the way back.

42:53.480 --> 42:56.270
Oh, my. Thank you.

43:01.590 --> 43:04.040
It's been a while since I bought them.

43:06.520 --> 43:10.190
Spiky, why are those girls wearing the same clothes?

43:10.960 --> 43:13.880
Oh, that's right! There's a summer festival tonight.

43:16.200 --> 43:18.460
And I wanted to see the fireworks...

43:19.180 --> 43:20.320
Fireworks?

43:21.330 --> 43:22.590
I wanna see fireworks!

43:23.270 --> 43:25.080
I wanna show Yoyo-chi the fireworks!

43:25.450 --> 43:27.650
Now's not a good time, Aki.

43:45.500 --> 43:46.450
So, how is it?

43:46.450 --> 43:48.740
Now that we're here, we've got to enjoy it!

43:49.690 --> 43:50.890
H-Hey!

43:54.740 --> 43:56.050
Not very good, are you?

43:56.590 --> 43:58.030
Let's see you do better, then.

43:58.590 --> 43:59.480
Fine.

44:01.980 --> 44:03.700
You can't use magic, though.

44:04.190 --> 44:05.710
That's what I hoped you'd say.

44:05.710 --> 44:07.410
I just do this...

44:09.650 --> 44:10.340
Huh?

44:16.320 --> 44:19.230
I told you that it's not easy. Just give up already!

44:19.770 --> 44:21.070
This is frustrating.

44:21.920 --> 44:23.700
Teach me how!

44:28.260 --> 44:29.550
So close.

44:29.550 --> 44:31.050
Teach me more!

44:31.910 --> 44:33.030
It's your posture.

44:33.600 --> 44:34.860
My posture?

44:35.480 --> 44:38.280
Tuck your elbows in tight and aim for the bottom.

44:39.300 --> 44:41.790
Here I go! This time for sure.

44:45.540 --> 44:46.890
I did it!

44:48.780 --> 44:50.270
I did it! I did it!

44:51.680 --> 44:54.330
That was a hard one to knock down. You did really well.

44:55.210 --> 44:56.380
I'm Yoyo, after all.

44:58.880 --> 44:59.430
Here.

45:02.730 --> 45:04.130
You wanted this, right?

45:06.230 --> 45:08.310
Th-Thank you.

45:15.040 --> 45:18.290
So how was it? Bet it was fun, even without magic.

45:19.020 --> 45:20.380
So-so, I guess.

45:20.380 --> 45:21.750
Whaddaya mean by that?

45:28.140 --> 45:29.950
Hey, Aki...

45:30.770 --> 45:31.450
Here.

45:32.680 --> 45:33.640
What's this?

45:35.830 --> 45:37.350
A band-aid.

45:37.900 --> 45:40.210
Put it on. I don't want to see it.

45:45.920 --> 45:47.050
Fireworks!

45:50.720 --> 45:51.710
So it's started.

45:52.830 --> 45:53.570
Let's go.

45:58.970 --> 46:00.640
That one just now looked like a face.

46:01.070 --> 46:03.070
I wonder how they make them do that.

46:04.320 --> 46:07.010
I'd like to show these to Nene-chan sometime.

46:16.580 --> 46:19.480
We have an announcement for the attendees.

46:20.500 --> 46:25.540
Unfortunately, due to technical difficulties, the fireworks will be delayed.

46:26.140 --> 46:29.080
Please be patient until we begin again.

46:30.010 --> 46:32.560
We have an announcement for the attendees.

46:30.370 --> 46:32.760
They stopped the fireworks?

46:32.560 --> 46:34.890
Unfortunately, due to technical difficulties, the fireworks will be delayed.

46:32.760 --> 46:34.890
What? You're telling me we have to wait?

46:35.570 --> 46:37.590
Times like this are what games are for.

46:37.590 --> 46:39.150
Get any more rare cards?

46:39.480 --> 46:40.010
Look!

46:57.290 --> 46:58.450
Hey, that's...

46:58.920 --> 46:59.620
It's happening!

47:08.350 --> 47:10.140
No. Something's different.

47:24.010 --> 47:25.610
What's going on!?

47:32.850 --> 47:34.370
Yoyo! Where are you goi—

47:44.660 --> 47:45.640
Aki!

47:48.630 --> 47:49.670
Someone!

47:51.260 --> 47:52.580
Yoyo!

48:02.870 --> 48:03.980
They're disappearing?

48:09.590 --> 48:10.510
What!?

48:16.280 --> 48:18.640
My poor forest...

48:28.390 --> 48:32.430
Seems someone is tryin' to pick a fight with the Kingdom of Magic.

48:33.120 --> 48:35.260
Everyone, please listen!

48:37.170 --> 48:38.810
Spiky! The buildings are—

48:39.190 --> 48:41.050
Where have you been!?

48:41.560 --> 48:42.600
Like I was saying—

48:42.600 --> 48:44.460
Aki got hurt!

48:45.280 --> 48:48.500
Oh, no! Want me to heal her with magic?

48:48.500 --> 48:50.280
She could have died!

48:50.930 --> 48:52.280
What good is your magic?

48:54.250 --> 48:59.200
Why are you mad? As long as you have the body, resurrection isn't a problem.

49:01.350 --> 49:04.480
That's not how things work! You idiot!

49:05.360 --> 49:08.850
What do you mean idiot, brat!?

49:08.850 --> 49:10.920
Well, you can forget about dispelling the curse!

49:11.320 --> 49:13.600
Like I actually expected you to!

49:13.600 --> 49:17.460
All the magic you've done so far has been pretty useless!

49:17.920 --> 49:19.380
Room for one more!

49:19.380 --> 49:21.490
Ah, that's us! We're coming.

49:21.970 --> 49:23.690
Aki, let's go.

49:28.100 --> 49:33.460
Hmph! How rude. They make picture books about <i>this</i> magical girl, you know?

49:34.220 --> 49:35.340
Right, Bihaku?

49:40.640 --> 49:41.530
Bihaku?

49:48.180 --> 49:50.820
This is where Yoyo-san was sent to the other world.

49:54.400 --> 49:55.840
These markings...

49:58.160 --> 49:59.510
Do you recognize them?

50:00.000 --> 50:02.150
Are they?

50:02.150 --> 50:02.930
Huh?

50:03.390 --> 50:07.290
This is the same as the portal that was opened twelve years ago.

50:07.840 --> 50:11.820
But the activation and continual use of it requires a considerable amount of magic power.

50:12.690 --> 50:14.440
Bihaku!

50:27.910 --> 50:28.720
Hoi!

50:34.320 --> 50:35.630
Are you all right?

50:42.540 --> 50:43.640
Bihaku?

50:57.040 --> 50:57.550
Hoi!

51:06.800 --> 51:07.620
Huh?

51:08.410 --> 51:11.850
That's strange. One more time...

51:14.340 --> 51:14.980
Hoi!

51:26.950 --> 51:28.040
Just now...

51:29.400 --> 51:33.600
Bihaku! Bihaku, aren't you going to wake up?

51:51.330 --> 51:55.120
This is strange. This is strange!

51:55.120 --> 51:56.150
This is...

52:25.210 --> 52:28.980
The Kingdom of Magic. I have to get back to the Kingdom of Magic!

52:49.620 --> 52:50.690
What!?

53:07.620 --> 53:09.040
H-Hey!

53:09.040 --> 53:09.990
What was that?

53:09.990 --> 53:11.110
It's a kid.

53:11.900 --> 53:12.720
Why?

53:13.870 --> 53:15.280
Hey, are you all right?

53:16.880 --> 53:19.330
What happened?

53:25.140 --> 53:27.270
Bihaku! Bihaku!

53:28.550 --> 53:30.740
Hey! You should stay still!

53:30.740 --> 53:33.080
Let me go! Bihaku!

53:34.140 --> 53:34.990
What is this?

53:35.910 --> 53:36.770
Hey, is this a cat?

53:37.090 --> 53:39.180
Don't touch him! Bihaku...

53:40.210 --> 53:42.930
Please move out of the way!

53:44.280 --> 53:46.510
Are you all right? Now—

53:47.580 --> 53:48.270
Bihaku.

53:49.920 --> 53:50.940
Bihaku is...

53:52.670 --> 53:55.210
I think she means this.

53:55.210 --> 53:57.670
But, is it even still alive?

53:57.670 --> 53:58.880
He's not gone!

53:59.650 --> 54:01.220
If I get to the Kingdom of Magic...

54:02.520 --> 54:03.550
I have to get back!

54:13.490 --> 54:17.600
Could you let me take a look for a second? I won't hurt him.

54:18.260 --> 54:23.570
I'll do what I can. But in return you have to accept medical attention.

55:09.740 --> 55:11.160
Yeah!

55:14.380 --> 55:15.330
Bihaku!

55:18.170 --> 55:19.500
Thank you!

55:20.210 --> 55:21.470
I'm glad I could help.

55:23.060 --> 55:24.380
It's like magic.

55:25.280 --> 55:26.130
Magic?

55:28.450 --> 55:31.050
If it's magic, then you're the one who cast it.

55:32.950 --> 55:36.840
I was able to save him because you didn't give up.

55:40.440 --> 55:42.260
That's great, isn't it?

55:42.260 --> 55:44.260
Oh, so it was a cat?

55:44.260 --> 55:46.220
Isn't this your sandal?

55:47.340 --> 55:48.490
Thank you.

55:54.900 --> 55:55.970
Takahiro...

55:56.520 --> 56:00.720
I want to find the boy and little girl that I was with!

56:10.690 --> 56:11.720
Thank you.

56:12.230 --> 56:14.570
Hey, you need a proper checkup, too!

56:15.090 --> 56:17.070
Dont'cha worry, I'm fine.

56:19.280 --> 56:20.580
Jeez.

56:22.440 --> 56:25.940
I'm telling you, this is way bigger than the missing monkey.

56:29.780 --> 56:32.820
Here you can see the sites of buildings that have vanished.

56:33.370 --> 56:37.640
The foundation is all that's left, as you can see here.

56:36.940 --> 56:38.050
They're not here.

56:39.980 --> 56:42.190
Thank goodness! It wasn't anything serious.

56:45.330 --> 56:46.390
Takahiro.

56:50.180 --> 56:50.760
What's wrong?

56:52.050 --> 56:53.090
Yoyo-chi.

57:37.010 --> 57:37.930
This is...

57:38.850 --> 57:40.000
Again!?

57:51.630 --> 57:52.990
It's coming this way!

58:08.610 --> 58:09.060
Hoi!

58:21.140 --> 58:21.700
Ei!

58:28.900 --> 58:29.400
Hoi!

58:35.990 --> 58:36.790
Yoyo did that?

58:59.970 --> 59:01.640
I can keep going!

59:04.540 --> 59:05.810
Amazing!

59:18.110 --> 59:19.450
I won't...

59:22.410 --> 59:23.330
Yoyo!

59:23.330 --> 59:24.490
I won't...

59:25.450 --> 59:29.710
Don't think for even a moment that I'll lose!

59:56.860 --> 59:57.670
Yoyo!

1:00:07.510 --> 1:00:10.040
Yoyo-chi... Is she okay?

1:00:15.950 --> 1:00:17.770
So she protected us.

1:00:27.070 --> 1:00:29.140
Her hair and eyes turned black?

1:00:29.920 --> 1:00:32.780
That's right. Then she collapsed.

1:00:35.220 --> 1:00:36.510
Surely, her magic hasn't...

1:00:37.310 --> 1:00:39.240
What in the world happened?

1:00:40.760 --> 1:00:42.260
Nene, move over.

1:00:44.020 --> 1:00:50.250
Hey, brat! I'm gettin' pretty fed up with your buildings falling all over the damn place and causing a ruckus.

1:00:50.920 --> 1:00:52.250
Get on and fix it!

1:00:54.140 --> 1:00:55.000
Who?

1:00:55.520 --> 1:00:57.130
I'm Oyone!

1:00:58.200 --> 1:00:59.200
So cool.

1:01:00.050 --> 1:01:02.230
W-Wait a second!

1:01:02.230 --> 1:01:04.140
We don't have any idea what's going on, either.

1:01:04.140 --> 1:01:08.120
With so much damage in just one day,
we've mobilized the entire kingdom to help.

1:01:08.120 --> 1:01:13.480
If you guys are planning some world-domination crap,
then you're in for a world of hurt.

1:01:13.480 --> 1:01:15.440
Things are bad here, too, ya know!

1:01:15.900 --> 1:01:18.210
Like I care about the status quo over there.

1:01:18.210 --> 1:01:21.450
I'll give you one day. Understand?

1:01:21.450 --> 1:01:22.530
<i>One</i> day!

1:01:22.530 --> 1:01:26.070
Oyone-san, Yoyo-san is there, too!

1:01:26.500 --> 1:01:28.330
I'm sure she can manage on her own.

1:01:28.720 --> 1:01:30.200
Oyomi, we're leaving.

1:01:30.200 --> 1:01:32.530
Begin preparations for the Pumpkin Party to commence battle.

1:01:33.060 --> 1:01:34.000
Yes, milady.

1:01:44.080 --> 1:01:44.990
Bihaku.

1:01:46.860 --> 1:01:48.490
So this is heaven?

1:01:54.600 --> 1:01:55.180
Yoyo!

1:01:56.770 --> 1:01:58.450
Ah, Takahiro!

1:01:58.920 --> 1:02:00.310
So, everyone is okay!

1:02:02.850 --> 1:02:04.120
Nene-chan!

1:02:04.820 --> 1:02:08.600
Yoyo-san! You're awake now!?

1:02:08.600 --> 1:02:10.830
Oh, it really did turn black.

1:02:13.300 --> 1:02:14.240
A thermometer?

1:02:14.800 --> 1:02:17.330
It's a magimeter for checking magic power levels.

1:02:18.950 --> 1:02:20.460
Wow! It's so high!

1:02:21.280 --> 1:02:24.170
Just as I feared, her magic is draining away.

1:02:26.060 --> 1:02:28.700
Yoyo-san's magic is limitless.

1:02:28.700 --> 1:02:31.680
It usually reads at least two hundred and fifty percent.

1:02:32.270 --> 1:02:38.770
At this rate... she might not even be able to return to our world.

1:02:40.370 --> 1:02:46.220
You've got to figure out how to get back here before Oyone-san goes on the offensive.

1:02:48.580 --> 1:02:49.570
Yoyo...

1:03:01.010 --> 1:03:04.800
Oyone-san's magic is powerful enough to destroy a world.

1:03:07.190 --> 1:03:11.140
And the job you hired me for hasn't even been completed.

1:03:14.960 --> 1:03:19.970
In that case, I'd better get started on those curses and stop Oyone-san's attack before it begins.

1:03:23.870 --> 1:03:24.680
Yoyo.

1:03:26.250 --> 1:03:28.650
Nene-chan, I need your help.

1:03:31.960 --> 1:03:32.900
Yoyo-san.

1:03:37.770 --> 1:03:42.040
The Miracle Stones might be the cause of these increasingly destructive events.

1:03:43.070 --> 1:03:49.090
They're are a twin set of stones that resonate more intensely the farther they are apart.

1:03:49.520 --> 1:03:55.020
The cause of these increasingly destructive events might be the work of two miracle stones

1:03:55.900 --> 1:03:57.880
Hey! We're ready!

1:03:57.880 --> 1:03:59.300
I'll be right there!

1:04:02.250 --> 1:04:03.690
I have something I want you to see.

1:04:06.700 --> 1:04:08.630
This one is from Tokyo.

1:04:09.170 --> 1:04:10.150
But there are more.

1:04:11.870 --> 1:04:13.240
The whole world!?

1:04:14.180 --> 1:04:19.560
Next, if you compare the distribution of events with users of that game...

1:04:22.740 --> 1:04:24.250
It's a perfect match!

1:04:24.840 --> 1:04:29.630
There may be a connection between the
disappearances and that symbol in the game.

1:04:29.630 --> 1:04:32.550
Here's the staff list for the company that created it.

1:04:32.720 --> 1:04:32.800
Production Staff

1:04:32.720 --> 1:04:32.800
Director & Creator: Nishiura Ishiki

1:04:34.170 --> 1:04:35.640
It's Papa!

1:04:36.900 --> 1:04:38.470
Great work, Long Hair!

1:04:38.990 --> 1:04:41.590
That means we know just where to go!

1:04:49.680 --> 1:04:51.700
It's no good. Their lines are down.

1:04:52.030 --> 1:04:53.610
Takahiro, it's up to you now.

1:04:57.340 --> 1:04:59.270
Where's the road!?

1:04:59.270 --> 1:05:00.980
Takahiro, keep going.

1:05:01.450 --> 1:05:02.070
Hoi!

1:05:09.780 --> 1:05:12.500
Wh-What should I do!?

1:05:12.500 --> 1:05:13.860
Calm down.

1:05:13.860 --> 1:05:16.580
You can do it! There's no need to be afraid.

1:05:17.670 --> 1:05:18.680
All right...

1:05:20.020 --> 1:05:21.720
I'm trusting you!

1:05:32.970 --> 1:05:34.360
What is that?

1:05:34.360 --> 1:05:36.000
Trees are growing right out of the building!

1:05:36.610 --> 1:05:39.170
Takahiro! We can get in through there.

1:05:50.000 --> 1:05:52.130
We're in! Bro, where are we going!?

1:05:52.560 --> 1:05:54.880
I think it was... the thirty-third floor!

1:05:55.340 --> 1:05:56.700
Yoyo! Let's go!

1:06:05.130 --> 1:06:07.870
It won't budge. Yoyo, use your magic.

1:06:08.900 --> 1:06:09.830
Hoi!

1:06:15.840 --> 1:06:17.280
It's open, Nishihiro-san!

1:06:17.820 --> 1:06:18.410
Huh?

1:06:19.630 --> 1:06:21.790
Huh, Takahiro-kun?

1:06:22.540 --> 1:06:23.690
Why are you here?

1:06:23.690 --> 1:06:25.200
Never mind that, uncle!

1:06:25.660 --> 1:06:27.870
You've gotta shut down the game!

1:06:28.380 --> 1:06:31.170
This world and the Kingdom of Magic are in danger!

1:06:31.560 --> 1:06:33.000
Kingdom of Magic?

1:06:34.010 --> 1:06:36.300
Huh? Who are you?

1:06:37.120 --> 1:06:39.780
So you're saying my game has something to do with all this?

1:06:41.090 --> 1:06:42.870
No, that can't be...

1:06:43.530 --> 1:06:46.980
Weird things only happen where that game is being played!

1:06:47.680 --> 1:06:52.710
This game... just uses magic to make people happy.

1:06:54.480 --> 1:06:56.320
What do you mean by that?

1:06:57.670 --> 1:07:01.700
Human beings have magical powers, some more than others.

1:07:02.400 --> 1:07:05.000
Would you believe me, Takahiro-kun, if I said that?

1:07:05.420 --> 1:07:07.120
We have magic power!?

1:07:07.600 --> 1:07:11.490
But in this world, magic disperses quickly.

1:07:12.130 --> 1:07:13.970
So people think it doesn't exist.

1:07:14.670 --> 1:07:17.880
Nao slowly lost her magic, too.

1:07:18.850 --> 1:07:20.180
So that's why my magic is...

1:07:21.060 --> 1:07:25.060
She then came up with a way to preserve some of that magic.

1:07:25.960 --> 1:07:29.380
I took that magic and incorporated it into my game.

1:07:28.810 --> 1:07:28.850
Noteworthy Auction - All auctions

1:07:28.810 --> 1:07:28.850
Card that grants wishs  Unused

1:07:33.320 --> 1:07:35.280
Magic from the Miracle Stone!

1:07:36.570 --> 1:07:37.780
You know about it?

1:07:37.780 --> 1:07:40.450
Papa-san! Where is the stone?

1:07:42.820 --> 1:07:43.840
Uncle!

1:07:44.610 --> 1:07:45.550
That's...

1:07:48.310 --> 1:07:49.300
It's snowing!

1:07:49.940 --> 1:07:51.210
Huh!?

1:07:54.240 --> 1:07:55.070
Snow!?

1:07:55.520 --> 1:07:56.710
In the summer?

1:08:01.510 --> 1:08:02.600
What now!?

1:08:19.380 --> 1:08:20.520
It's there.

1:08:22.990 --> 1:08:26.900
Nao's stone is over there.

1:08:43.390 --> 1:08:47.080
Yoyo-san, the situation is getting worse. There isn't much time.

1:08:49.810 --> 1:08:52.690
I'm going to destroy the stone. Is that okay?

1:08:56.470 --> 1:08:57.170
Let's get goin'.

1:09:48.120 --> 1:09:49.890
R-Robot!?

1:09:51.330 --> 1:09:52.950
It's protecting the stone?

1:09:56.840 --> 1:09:57.800
This is bad!

1:10:23.000 --> 1:10:24.150
H-Hey!

1:10:24.660 --> 1:10:26.020
What's wrong!?

1:10:34.850 --> 1:10:37.300
Nene-chan, this doesn't make sense.

1:10:37.300 --> 1:10:40.010
Isn't it strange, the way Yoyo is losing her magic?

1:10:40.480 --> 1:10:41.680
If this is...

1:10:43.280 --> 1:10:47.630
If this is because the stones are separated...

1:10:48.100 --> 1:10:51.680
then bringing them even slightly closer should weaken them.

1:10:58.260 --> 1:10:59.690
The Pumpkin Party!?

1:11:01.010 --> 1:11:02.110
Oyone-san?

1:11:08.240 --> 1:11:09.000
Yoyo!

1:11:21.040 --> 1:11:22.790
Yoyo. You...

1:11:24.140 --> 1:11:24.880
can't be...

1:11:30.680 --> 1:11:32.600
I think black suits me surprisingly well.

1:11:47.230 --> 1:11:48.360
Takahiro?

1:11:49.360 --> 1:11:52.160
Hold on tight!

1:11:52.530 --> 1:11:54.250
Sorry about this, Yoyo!

1:11:54.780 --> 1:11:58.490
I... I  promise you...

1:11:59.450 --> 1:12:04.460
Once this is over, I'll make sure you get back home!

1:12:04.460 --> 1:12:06.760
So... So...

1:12:08.890 --> 1:12:10.300
I'm not too heavy?

1:12:10.930 --> 1:12:12.140
Not at all!

1:12:17.330 --> 1:12:18.690
Hold up!

1:12:18.690 --> 1:12:19.570
What!?

1:12:19.570 --> 1:12:20.320
That!

1:12:24.230 --> 1:12:25.680
It's cursed water.

1:12:26.130 --> 1:12:27.480
Cursed water?

1:12:27.480 --> 1:12:29.730
Just touching it is enough to curse you.

1:12:30.250 --> 1:12:31.310
Let me down.

1:12:33.530 --> 1:12:34.390
Takahiro?

1:12:39.230 --> 1:12:40.480
This is so gross!

1:12:40.480 --> 1:12:41.670
Takahiro!

1:12:41.980 --> 1:12:44.980
What are you doing? Let me down!

1:12:45.470 --> 1:12:47.920
Your magic is getting weaker, isn't it!?

1:12:48.800 --> 1:12:51.990
We can't afford to use any of it here!

1:12:52.490 --> 1:12:55.870
If I get cursed, you can just fix me up

1:12:55.870 --> 1:12:57.930
once all of this is over.

1:13:01.770 --> 1:13:03.300
Target sighted!

1:13:04.280 --> 1:13:05.520
Prepare the attack!

1:13:05.970 --> 1:13:09.930
If we go all the way, we might not be able to return either.

1:13:10.440 --> 1:13:12.930
No resources are spared when administering justice.

1:13:12.930 --> 1:13:15.400
Everyone! Are preparations complete?

1:13:15.400 --> 1:13:16.550
Oyone-san!

1:13:21.520 --> 1:13:22.430
Nene?

1:13:34.020 --> 1:13:36.640
How was that? We made it.

1:13:37.480 --> 1:13:38.460
Takahiro...

1:14:04.020 --> 1:14:07.260
Nao. Was I wrong?

1:14:08.270 --> 1:14:11.830
Was it wrong to spread this magic?

1:14:16.580 --> 1:14:17.420
Keep going.

1:14:18.780 --> 1:14:19.530
But...

1:14:19.530 --> 1:14:20.990
Go on without me.

1:14:26.880 --> 1:14:30.080
But I don't have any magic power left.

1:14:31.150 --> 1:14:32.130
Run!

1:14:34.610 --> 1:14:37.190
If you can't fly, you still have legs, right?

1:14:37.890 --> 1:14:41.020
If you don't have a weapon, you have arms.

1:14:41.020 --> 1:14:44.460
If you don't have transportation, then run!

1:14:48.250 --> 1:14:52.170
H-How did I not see that?

1:14:55.590 --> 1:14:56.760
Thank you.

1:16:04.580 --> 1:16:05.830
Time's up.

1:16:05.830 --> 1:16:07.750
Wait just a little longer!

1:16:07.750 --> 1:16:12.420
Nene, you dare speak against the
Kingdom of Magic's High Commander?

1:16:12.920 --> 1:16:17.460
Yoyo-san has lost her magic and can't get back!

1:16:17.460 --> 1:16:19.300
If you attack now, then Yoyo-san will...

1:16:20.630 --> 1:16:22.970
In situations like these, we must take a stand for ourselves.

1:16:23.300 --> 1:16:25.310
But family comes first, right?

1:16:25.680 --> 1:16:26.930
Grandma!?

1:16:30.020 --> 1:16:33.730
How about we give her another twenty minutes, Sis?

1:16:37.610 --> 1:16:38.860
Make it happen in ten.

1:16:54.790 --> 1:16:56.040
I made it!

1:17:12.140 --> 1:17:14.310
So this is a Miracle Stone.

1:17:18.940 --> 1:17:20.530
It's at its limit.

1:17:28.910 --> 1:17:29.950
What is this!?

1:17:42.670 --> 1:17:44.590
I-It's huge!

1:17:50.520 --> 1:17:52.180
Oh my...

1:17:52.180 --> 1:17:53.180
Yoyo?

1:17:53.180 --> 1:17:55.600
It seems she got sucked into the curse.

1:17:56.400 --> 1:17:57.520
Why doesn't she just get out?

1:17:58.690 --> 1:18:00.980
She can't fight back without any magic.

1:18:01.820 --> 1:18:02.570
Takahiro-san!

1:18:03.240 --> 1:18:05.700
Can you send her even just a little magic power?

1:18:06.160 --> 1:18:08.200
You say that so casually,

1:18:09.120 --> 1:18:10.910
but how am I supposed to do that!?

1:18:13.660 --> 1:18:18.170
Kensei-kun, can you bring Aki here?

1:18:18.750 --> 1:18:20.380
Huh? Aki-chan?

1:18:20.710 --> 1:18:25.380
I'm counting on you! I can't control the game anymore. I can't stop it.

1:18:25.720 --> 1:18:30.140
If the stone goes berserk, we'll need Nao's power to hold it back.

1:18:30.140 --> 1:18:31.260
I wish she'd marry me.

1:18:30.140 --> 1:18:31.510
I'd like to wring the director's neck.

1:18:31.260 --> 1:18:32.560
They should all just disappear.

1:18:31.260 --> 1:18:32.560
I'm tired of them being around.

1:18:33.980 --> 1:18:36.140
What is this?

1:18:52.370 --> 1:18:53.450
Where...

1:18:59.130 --> 1:18:59.960
am I?

1:19:06.510 --> 1:19:08.930
It's cold. I'm hungry.

1:19:12.850 --> 1:19:14.930
Oh, I didn't see you there.

1:19:16.890 --> 1:19:19.060
Who'd have thought you could see them in the city?

1:19:35.950 --> 1:19:37.790
Takahiro-kun, can you hear me?

1:19:37.790 --> 1:19:41.540
Kensei-kun is on his way with Aki.

1:19:41.540 --> 1:19:43.170
Just stay put for now.

1:19:43.170 --> 1:19:44.710
He is!?

1:19:44.710 --> 1:19:46.130
"Stay put," you say—

1:20:11.110 --> 1:20:13.370
Nao-san?

1:20:16.160 --> 1:20:19.160
Earth's
history
from
a
rock's
perspective

1:20:39.930 --> 1:20:41.940
How to return Nao to her world

1:21:01.660 --> 1:21:05.040
These are... the stone's memories?

1:21:08.050 --> 1:21:10.130
He should be around here somewhere.

1:21:10.130 --> 1:21:11.550
Hey!

1:21:15.350 --> 1:21:16.390
Papa!

1:21:16.970 --> 1:21:17.850
Uncle!

1:21:17.850 --> 1:21:19.310
Papa!

1:21:19.310 --> 1:21:20.270
Aki!

1:21:22.310 --> 1:21:23.940
Thank you, Kensei-kun.

1:21:24.690 --> 1:21:25.650
Don't mention it.

1:21:27.480 --> 1:21:28.070
Let's go.

1:21:52.720 --> 1:21:54.930
Store magic power in the stone?

1:21:55.340 --> 1:21:58.510
Yes. But it would be impossible to fill on my own.

1:21:58.510 --> 1:22:01.470
So, I'll borrow everyone's magic power little by little.

1:22:02.140 --> 1:22:07.730
And I'll even grant a wish to the people I borrow from in return. How does that sound?

1:22:08.360 --> 1:22:09.730
Why would you do that?

1:22:10.690 --> 1:22:15.660
I always wanted to show her the kingdom where I grew up.

1:22:17.410 --> 1:22:18.240
I see.

1:22:19.450 --> 1:22:24.040
She's the magic I never expected and brings me true happiness.

1:22:25.210 --> 1:22:31.420
I want to give something back to the people of this world who have brought me so much happiness.

1:22:33.420 --> 1:22:35.010
I look forward to its completion.

1:22:48.940 --> 1:22:49.860
Papa!

1:22:52.980 --> 1:22:53.690
Aki.

1:22:53.690 --> 1:22:54.280
Huh?

1:22:55.110 --> 1:22:56.780
I want you to do something for me.

1:22:57.410 --> 1:22:59.990
Takahiro is waiting at the bottom of that tree.

1:23:00.990 --> 1:23:02.330
I want you to go to him.

1:23:09.330 --> 1:23:13.670
I'll plant the stone here before my magic power runs out.

1:23:14.300 --> 1:23:16.340
The place where we first met, huh?

1:23:17.590 --> 1:23:20.800
This tree will keep it safe.

1:23:21.930 --> 1:23:27.690
But I want to give a piece to Aki, to protect her as well.

1:23:28.600 --> 1:23:32.480
Don't be scared. Mama is sure to protect you.

1:23:33.360 --> 1:23:34.940
You're going to save everyone.

1:23:35.570 --> 1:23:36.440
Papa.

1:23:49.040 --> 1:23:53.210
Nao-san was only thinking of everyone's happiness.

1:23:55.920 --> 1:23:56.760
But...

1:24:00.220 --> 1:24:04.970
These people were only thinking of themselves.

1:24:06.350 --> 1:24:12.520
Even the most wholesome magic would become cursed against such selfish wishes.

1:24:17.440 --> 1:24:21.410
Everyone... Everyone is so selfish.

1:24:35.880 --> 1:24:35.920
I wish for my grandfather in the country be safe

1:24:45.600 --> 1:24:46.600
What are you doing?

1:24:48.060 --> 1:24:53.060
It probably won't work, but this app says it grants wishes.

1:24:54.020 --> 1:24:56.070
Like a little prayer, you know?

1:24:57.650 --> 1:25:01.950
Maybe I'll give it a try, too.

1:25:03.700 --> 1:25:03.740
I hope my daughter is safe.

1:25:04.700 --> 1:25:04.740
I hope that girl's
injuries heal over.

1:25:05.160 --> 1:25:05.200
I wish my wife and the doctors are well.

1:25:07.330 --> 1:25:07.370
I wish the doctor

1:25:07.330 --> 1:25:07.370
will be reunited with his family.

1:25:23.840 --> 1:25:23.890
I wish the boy who

1:25:23.840 --> 1:25:23.890
gave me his seat

1:25:23.840 --> 1:25:23.890
on the train is safe.

1:25:25.850 --> 1:25:25.890
is doing well.

1:25:25.850 --> 1:25:25.890
I hope the kid who saved my daughter

1:25:27.850 --> 1:25:27.890
I wish that everyone would smile.

1:25:42.110 --> 1:25:43.860
What's happening now?

1:25:57.710 --> 1:26:00.050
The stone's magic was released!?

1:26:19.150 --> 1:26:20.400
This is...

1:26:23.570 --> 1:26:25.700
Aki. Are you seeing this?

1:26:26.200 --> 1:26:29.660
This is what Mama wanted to show you.

1:26:53.430 --> 1:26:55.390
Didn't you destroy the stone?

1:27:00.360 --> 1:27:01.320
Aki!

1:27:02.730 --> 1:27:04.440
It was too late...

1:27:05.190 --> 1:27:06.860
The world is already...

1:27:16.460 --> 1:27:17.460
Nene-chan!

1:27:19.540 --> 1:27:20.840
Yoyo-san!

1:27:20.840 --> 1:27:24.380
I'm going to restore this world. Please, teach me how.

1:27:25.210 --> 1:27:27.300
If you use such large-scale spell—

1:27:27.300 --> 1:27:28.430
I won't be able to return.

1:27:31.800 --> 1:27:34.180
With the magic you have now, you could, though.

1:27:34.850 --> 1:27:38.770
Please come back, Yoyo-san!

1:27:40.770 --> 1:27:43.980
This is the magic power that everyone has bestowed upon me.

1:27:44.570 --> 1:27:45.990
I have to pay them back.

1:27:46.740 --> 1:27:53.280
Besides, the magical sisters have a one hundred percent satisfaction rate!

1:27:53.780 --> 1:27:55.040
Yoyo-san.

1:27:55.830 --> 1:27:56.830
Go for it.

1:27:58.080 --> 1:28:01.290
But if you fail, you know what will happen.

1:28:01.670 --> 1:28:05.050
I will destroy that world, Yoyo.

1:28:08.130 --> 1:28:11.050
I have faith in magic!

1:28:11.970 --> 1:28:14.720
Well, aren't you thick-headed?

1:28:16.140 --> 1:28:20.850
At this rate, that spiky haired boy will be able to use magic.

1:28:21.690 --> 1:28:26.150
Nene, even if you weren't born with magic power, that doesn't mean you can't use it.

1:28:48.050 --> 1:28:49.470
The magic power...

1:28:49.840 --> 1:28:51.840
It's all right, Aki is there.

1:28:52.300 --> 1:28:54.140
Nao's stone is inside her Pez dispenser.

1:28:54.600 --> 1:28:55.430
Bihaku?

1:28:56.510 --> 1:29:00.270
The stone inside holds the last bit of magic!

1:29:03.310 --> 1:29:05.020
Thank you, Bihaku!

1:29:06.360 --> 1:29:08.730
B-But will you make it in time?

1:29:09.070 --> 1:29:10.360
I've got to try.

1:29:11.200 --> 1:29:13.110
I'll worry about that later.

1:29:13.490 --> 1:29:15.490
I have no choice but to believe, right?

1:29:17.450 --> 1:29:19.120
Hold on, Yoyo-san!

1:29:19.120 --> 1:29:22.120
Takahiro-san is headed your way!

1:29:22.830 --> 1:29:25.540
Why do I always get stuck with the hard jobs?

1:29:33.090 --> 1:29:37.100
My legs!

1:29:37.100 --> 1:29:38.640
Now this is just ridiculous!

1:29:43.850 --> 1:29:45.350
Idiot!

1:30:06.080 --> 1:30:07.040
Bihaku?

1:30:27.860 --> 1:30:28.980
Time's up!

1:30:29.400 --> 1:30:30.520
Oyone-san!

1:30:30.520 --> 1:30:31.690
Shut it!

1:30:32.740 --> 1:30:34.320
Attack!

1:30:40.740 --> 1:30:42.040
Move the arms!

1:30:46.920 --> 1:30:48.630
Pierce through!

1:30:49.920 --> 1:30:51.050
Yoyo-san.

1:31:11.520 --> 1:31:12.320
Nene-chan!

1:31:39.840 --> 1:31:40.680
Almost there!

1:31:43.310 --> 1:31:44.220
Reach her!

1:31:45.640 --> 1:31:47.230
Yoyo!

1:31:55.280 --> 1:31:55.860
That's Mama's...

1:32:05.950 --> 1:32:06.620
Mama?

1:32:10.580 --> 1:32:12.420
On my mark! Prepare to fire!

1:32:12.420 --> 1:32:13.290
Sis?

1:32:15.590 --> 1:32:18.050
Take it!

1:32:18.050 --> 1:32:19.340
Our target: that over-sized tin can!

1:32:52.750 --> 1:32:53.250
Hoi!

1:33:25.370 --> 1:33:29.450
Your request... has been fulfilled.

1:33:43.930 --> 1:33:45.050
Are you finally awake?

1:33:48.640 --> 1:33:49.640
Where are we?

1:33:53.940 --> 1:33:56.730
I wonder when I got magic powers, too.

1:33:59.530 --> 1:34:06.240
I see. The magic from every creature is what makes this world go round.

1:34:07.910 --> 1:34:10.240
This magic was always here.

1:34:13.460 --> 1:34:16.540
You're saying this rainbow bridge was here all along, too?

1:34:18.920 --> 1:34:20.420
My heart is warm.

1:34:37.650 --> 1:34:38.270
Here.

1:34:43.400 --> 1:34:45.950
I don't have money for you, so take this instead.

1:34:48.200 --> 1:34:49.120
Thank you!

1:34:50.580 --> 1:34:54.370
At times like this, I think a tight hug is in order.

1:35:00.250 --> 1:35:01.460
I'll give you this.

1:35:01.920 --> 1:35:03.050
Are you sure?

1:35:04.840 --> 1:35:05.970
I don't need it now.

1:35:08.300 --> 1:35:10.050
Thank you for looking after me.

1:35:13.680 --> 1:35:15.230
You're welcome.

1:35:20.150 --> 1:35:21.730
Thank you, Yoyo.

1:35:26.240 --> 1:35:30.120
I... I believe in magic!

1:35:54.600 --> 1:35:57.020
I'm no longer needed in this world.

1:36:15.240 --> 1:36:17.250
itsuka oboetemasuka?

1:36:16.950 --> 1:36:17.250
Do you remember that story

1:36:18.960 --> 1:36:20.960
ehon mitai na sutouri

1:36:20.670 --> 1:36:20.960
that was like from a picture book?

1:36:22.670 --> 1:36:24.670
shinjita koto wasurete

1:36:24.340 --> 1:36:24.670
Leave behind what you believe

1:36:26.460 --> 1:36:28.470
mitakotonai sekai e to

1:36:28.170 --> 1:36:28.470
and come with me to a novel world...

1:36:45.110 --> 1:36:47.110
sore wa kimi no mae kara

1:36:46.820 --> 1:36:47.110
It was always right there in front of you

1:36:48.940 --> 1:36:50.950
inaku natta wake janai

1:36:50.650 --> 1:36:50.950
Never once had it been missing

1:36:52.660 --> 1:36:54.660
kurikaesenai shunkan

1:36:54.370 --> 1:36:54.660
That critical moment

1:36:56.450 --> 1:36:58.450
namidasuru imi o shirimashita

1:36:58.160 --> 1:36:58.450
taught me what it meant to cry

1:37:02.960 --> 1:37:04.960
kono itami ga

1:37:04.670 --> 1:37:04.960
If only someone had come

1:37:07.460 --> 1:37:09.460
dareka o sukueru no nara

1:37:09.170 --> 1:37:09.460
and saved me from that pain

1:37:14.930 --> 1:37:16.930
yureru yume maboroshi

1:37:16.640 --> 1:37:16.930
I was like a shade, swept away

1:37:22.690 --> 1:37:24.690
guuzen no kotoba sae

1:37:24.400 --> 1:37:24.690
by the most improbable of words

1:37:24.610 --> 1:37:26.610
negai kanadeta kiseki kakenukeru sora

1:37:26.270 --> 1:37:26.610
to chase after miracles in the night sky

1:37:30.320 --> 1:37:31.320
youkoso shinfonii

1:37:31.320 --> 1:37:31.320
A welcoming symphony

1:37:33.410 --> 1:37:33.570
A simple song can

1:37:34.240 --> 1:37:35.490
fushigi datte odoruyo

1:37:35.240 --> 1:37:35.490
inspire a wondrous dance

1:37:35.490 --> 1:37:38.660
inspire a wondrous dance

1:37:37.910 --> 1:37:38.990
futatsu no riezon

1:37:38.910 --> 1:37:38.990
Us two liaisons

1:37:39.910 --> 1:37:41.120
guuzen janai

1:37:40.910 --> 1:37:41.120
are not here by chance

1:37:41.750 --> 1:37:42.920
supairaru tadoreba saa

1:37:42.750 --> 1:37:42.920
here, spiraling together

1:37:46.170 --> 1:37:47.420
tokihanatte uso no nai negai dake o

1:37:47.170 --> 1:37:47.420
Set time adrift with only one true wish.

1:37:54.130 --> 1:37:54.260
It's time to set things in motion

1:37:55.800 --> 1:37:56.010
and the time has come for

1:37:57.680 --> 1:37:57.850
the ultimate magic

1:38:00.350 --> 1:38:00.770
to grant that wish

1:38:03.940 --> 1:38:05.940
"yume miruno, yamemashita"

1:38:05.650 --> 1:38:05.940
"Give up on your dreams."

1:38:07.730 --> 1:38:09.730
otona, sukoshi waratte

1:38:09.400 --> 1:38:09.730
Looking back, I smile a little

1:38:11.440 --> 1:38:13.450
okizari no jikan mada

1:38:13.150 --> 1:38:13.450
I've turned my back on my childish days

1:38:15.200 --> 1:38:17.200
kodomo, no mama nagareru namida

1:38:16.910 --> 1:38:17.200
when I could only weep

1:38:21.700 --> 1:38:23.710
sotto yudaneta

1:38:23.410 --> 1:38:23.710
I slowly devoted myself

1:38:26.210 --> 1:38:28.210
omoi wa dare no tame darou

1:38:27.920 --> 1:38:28.210
to supporting other people's feelings

1:38:33.720 --> 1:38:35.720
yugamu

1:38:35.430 --> 1:38:35.720
I struggled

1:38:36.680 --> 1:38:38.680
yume no naka de

1:38:38.390 --> 1:38:38.680
within my own dreams

1:38:41.430 --> 1:38:43.430
kiete wa umarekawaru

1:38:43.140 --> 1:38:43.430
What's annihilated will be recreated

1:38:43.310 --> 1:38:45.310
kimi no senaka o koete ryoute kazasu sora

1:38:45.020 --> 1:38:45.310
Raise yourself to stand above the skies

1:38:49.060 --> 1:38:50.070
kasanaru shinpashii

1:38:50.070 --> 1:38:50.070
Interwoven sympathy

1:38:52.190 --> 1:38:52.320
If I purse my lips

1:38:52.320 --> 1:38:52.570
kuchi zu sameba

1:38:53.030 --> 1:38:54.280
mujakina hi modoru yo

1:38:54.030 --> 1:38:54.280
I can return to more innocent days

1:38:56.570 --> 1:38:57.780
negai no riizun

1:38:57.570 --> 1:38:57.780
The purpose of my wish

1:38:58.740 --> 1:38:59.870
mienai youni

1:38:59.740 --> 1:38:59.870
is to take the unseen

1:39:00.450 --> 1:39:01.740
karafuru ni egakou mada,

1:39:01.450 --> 1:39:01.740
and paint it with colors

1:39:05.000 --> 1:39:06.160
kidzukanai de kimi ni tsuita uso dake wa

1:39:06.000 --> 1:39:06.160
You may not know, but the lies tucked away

1:39:11.800 --> 1:39:12.920
saigen no nai toki ga kite mo

1:39:12.800 --> 1:39:12.920
veiled by the never-ending flow of time

1:39:15.420 --> 1:39:16.590
saigo no mahou tokeru made

1:39:16.430 --> 1:39:16.590
